 },
 "paragraphs": [
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p001.s01",
     "source": "1."
    },
    {
     "id": "p001.s02",
     "source": "Turn to the right, or turn to the left, ’Twill all be one in the end."
    }
   ],
   "id": "p001"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p002.s01",
     "source": "2."
    },
    {
     "id": "p002.s02",
     "source": "The rat that came from outside, Drove out the house-born rat."
    }
   ],
   "id": "p002"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p003.s01",
     "source": "3."
    },
    {
     "id": "p003.s02",
     "source": "Fight for the outlying village, If thou wantest the one nearer home."
    }
   ],
   "id": "p003"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p004.s01",
     "source": "4."
    },
    {
     "id": "p004.s02",
     "source": "Wish thy neighbour to have an ox, And God will send it to thee."
    }
   ],
   "id": "p004"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p005.s01",
     "source": "5."
    },
    {
     "id": "p005.s02",
     "source": "The wolf was abused as wolfish, While the jackal ate up the flock."
    }
   ],
   "id": "p005"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p006.s01",
     "source": "6."
    },
    {
     "id": "p006.s02",
     "source": "The hen scratched and scratched till she dug up a knife, With which her own throat was afterwards cut."
    }
   ],
   "id": "p006"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p007.s01",
     "source": "7."
    },
    {
     "id": "p007.s02",
     "source": "The road runs where an old road ran, The river flows in the bed of a former river."
    }
   ],
   "id": "p007"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p008.s01",
     "source": "8."
    },
    {
     "id": "p008.s02",
     "source": "‘Give me room to stand,’ quoth the bull, ‘and I Shall make myself enough room to lie.’"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p008"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p009.s01",
     "source": "9."
    },
    {
     "id": "p009.s02",
     "source": "If the bear overcome thee—then call him Papa."
    }
   ],
   "id": "p009"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p010.s01",
     "source": "10."
    },
    {
     "id": "p010.s02",
     "source": "The dog took fright at a wolf, And barked all the year round at a stump."
    }
   ],
   "id": "p010"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p011.s01",
     "source": "11."
    },
    {
     "id": "p011.s02",
     "source": "Who ever heard of a fish being prized As long as it stayed in the stream?"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p011"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p012.s01",
     "source": "12."
    },
    {
     "id": "p012.s02",
     "source": "They shot at the ripe—but the green fruit fell."
    }
   ],
   "id": "p012"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p013.s01",
     "source": "13."
    },
    {
     "id": "p013.s02",
     "source": "Leave a good deed on a stone by the way, Thou’lt find it again after many a day ( i.e. Cast thy bread on the waters)."
    }
   ],
   "id": "p013"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p014.s01",
     "source": "14."
    },
    {
     "id": "p014.s02",
     "source": "I say it—but whether it happen or no ’Tis nothing to do with me."
    }
   ],
   "id": "p014"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p015.s01",
     "source": "15."
    },
    {
     "id": "p015.s02",
     "source": "Eat and drink up whatever is thine, But cross thyself over all that’s mine."
    }
   ],
   "id": "p015"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p016.s01",
     "source": "16."
    },
    {
     "id": "p016.s02",
     "source": "Who slew me?—My brother."
    },
    {
     "id": "p016.s03",
     "source": "Who brought me back to life?—My brother."
    }
   ],
   "id": "p016"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p017.s01",
     "source": "17."
    },
    {
     "id": "p017.s02",
     "source": "The well-doer receives not good in return."
    }
   ],
   "id": "p017"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p018.s01",
     "source": "18."
    },
    {
     "id": "p018.s02",
     "source": "The truthful man is always duped."
    }
   ],
   "id": "p018"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p019.s01",
     "source": "19."
    },
    {
     "id": "p019.s02",
     "source": "My father I love, my mother I love— But myself I prefer before all."
    }
   ],
   "id": "p019"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p020.s01",
     "source": "20."
    },
    {
     "id": "p020.s02",
     "source": "A heart-kiss is better than a lip-kiss."
    }
   ],
   "id": "p020"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p021.s01",
     "source": "21."
    },
    {
     "id": "p021.s02",
     "source": "If thou hast not eaten pepper, why does thy mouth burn?"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p021"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p022.s01",
     "source": "22."
    },
    {
     "id": "p022.s02",
     "source": "A disease that one sees, will not kill; ’Tis hidden sores do the most ill."
    }
   ],
   "id": "p022"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p023.s01",
     "source": "23."
    },
    {
     "id": "p023.s02",
     "source": "Our granny has no teeth, so she Likes not others’ teeth to see."
    }
   ],
   "id": "p023"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p024.s01",
     "source": "24."
    },
    {
     "id": "p024.s02",
     "source": "He has forgotten the soul of his father, so he swears by the soul of his grandsire."
    }
   ],
   "id": "p024"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p025.s01",
     "source": "25."
    },
    {
     "id": "p025.s02",
     "source": "Gold is good, but if thou have it not, of what use is it to thee?"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p025"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p026.s01",
     "source": "26."
    },
    {
     "id": "p026.s02",
     "source": "Better is copper of thine own than gold that is another’s."
    }
   ],
   "id": "p026"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p027.s01",
     "source": "27."
    },
    {
     "id": "p027.s02",
     "source": "Of what use is light to him that is blind?"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p027"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p028.s01",
     "source": "28."
    },
    {
     "id": "p028.s02",
     "source": "If thou art brave, do not bewail The bluntness of thy sword."
    }
   ],
   "id": "p028"
  },
  {
   "type": "break",
   "segments": [],
   "id": "p029"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p030.s01",
     "source": "Cf. note 3 on p. 109."
    }
   ],
   "id": "p030"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p031.s01",
     "source": "Cf. The Talmud (Polano’s Selections , p. 287)."
    },
    {
     "id": "p031.s02",
     "source": "‘If the fox is king bow before him.’"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p031"
  }
 ]
}